Z||000000||Gerald||10-20-2001||11:10 PM||||my engine wont turn over at all. The starter worked fine for as long as ive had the car but today when i finished filling the tank it would not crank. Not even a click, the battery is less nthen a week old. Could it be the clutch safety switch? Or can a starter die with absoluty no warning. It worked perfect untill today.<P>if it helps my car is a 87 4cyl DIS coupe with the 5 spd||||reg||8
Z||000001||85 gt fiero||10-20-2001||11:20 PM||||Check your battery connections one of the wires may be bad or its lose, also check your fuses, i doubt it but it may need an alternator, or a cylinode.  Hope you get it fixe. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   Randy<P>------------------<BR>RALLY CAR, FULL ROLL CAGE, SKID PLATES AND SOON TO BE BRIGHT YELLOW||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||10-21-2001||08:01 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Gerald:<BR><B>my engine wont turn over at all. The starter worked fine for as long as ive had the car but today when i finished filling the tank it would not crank. Not even a click, the battery is less nthen a week old. Could it be the clutch safety switch? Or can a starter die with absoluty no warning. It worked perfect untill today.<P>if it helps my car is a 87 4cyl DIS coupe with the 5 spd</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Check the bottom stud on the solenoid, you will see a strap running from it to the starter body, it may be broken...<P>Jumper the top stud to the bottom stud and see if the starter turns over (out of gear!)...<P>If the starter solenoid is bad, and it happens, you will get no click, but the starter will spin up when you jump the top and bottom studs...<P>If the starter is bad, it will not spin...<BR><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">        <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||walsh2001||10-22-2001||09:35 AM||||My 2 cents... something like this happened on my 84. Check the wires going to the starter... at one point, mine melted off (heat from the exhaust manifold.) If it is not that, did you try rocking it in gear? Perhaps the gear is stuck on the flywheel.<P>You could try putting voltage directly on the starter to see if it will turn... put it on a bench and test it. Worse case scenario (assuming it is the starter) the starter is shot.<P>------------------<BR>'87 Fiero GT ... Cherry Red||||reg||1
